{
  "artifacts": {
    "plan": {
      "summary": "Implement durable Goal decisions, settlements and recovery history on the clean Round 2 base f880b7767149e4de43d5bc4d4786247d1e536a8c. Selectively adapt Round 1 work to current Skills execution, deferred transitions and exact-candidate approval. Keep integration separate from acceptance, preserve history through synchronization and deletion, and expose indexed CLI/API metrics.",
      "checklist": [
        {
          "id": "P1",
          "description": "Use the supplied Round 2 worktree throughout implementation and verification. Selectively reuse Round 1 outcome types, decision validation, archive handling and fixture ideas after reassessment; replace its automatic-completion inference and persistence hooks. Preserve the entire Round 1 worktree, branch, uncommitted files and historical artifacts. Leave integration, workflow advancement and serving-installation operations to Refine."
        },
        {
          "id": "P2",
          "description": "Add backward-compatible audit types in focused model/goal modules: immutable human decisions, terminal outcomes, recovery/reopening events and explicit completion authority. Decisions carry stable event/request identities, Goal, one-based Round, node, reviewer, original decision time, accepted/rejected result, optional reason and exact candidate. Outcomes capture completion time, resolution, failure category/evidence, intervention, Round counts and first-Round success. Capture Goal reporter and Feature attribution at occurrence time, independently of reviewer identity."
        },
        {
          "id": "P3",
          "description": "Add shared decision and settlement operations under application/work_items. Require request ID, explicit human provenance, reviewer and expected node, Round, candidate and revision/generation. Identical retries return the original receipt/event without changing timestamps; conflicting reuse and stale submissions fail without mutation. Commit decision, status, outcome and current-outcome reference in one durable Goal replacement under existing record locks and revision fencing. Validate immutable identities and causal references on every audit-bearing write."
        },
        {
          "id": "P4",
          "description": "Compose decisions with current Event transition gates. Persist a fenced pending request and original submission time when Skills defer a transition; expose pending separately from completion. Materialize the decision and terminal outcome atomically only when the transition actually settles, retaining decided_at and assigning completed_at at settlement. Deferred execution must revalidate ownership, revision, candidate and approval proof. Failed, cancelled or superseded gates retain request and Skill evidence without creating a completed acceptance. Never hold Goal locks while Skills execute."
        },
        {
          "id": "P5",
          "description": "Move review orchestration into the shared work-item capability and extract/reuse the existing integration-proof helper. Acceptance must retain successful exact-candidate integration, target ancestry and required publication checks, with proof and Goal identity fenced through final commit using established lock ordering. Rejection requires the reviewed exact candidate but does not need successful acceptance proof. Approval never integrates again. Generic status writes cannot create Done or Rejected without corresponding authorized evidence."
        },
        {
          "id": "P6",
          "description": "Add Rejected to workflow serialization, operations, projections, filters, browser presentation and the Skills trigger catalog. Rejected is settled, unsuccessful and unschedulable; like Failed, it holds ordered Feature work until explicit recovery. Preserve existing Review ordering behavior and Feature final-state rollup semantics while exposing rejected counts separately from successful completion. Support an explicit new Round from the current target after rejection, retaining integrated code and the rejection. Cancellation remains distinct."
        },
        {
          "id": "P7",
          "description": "Route CLI approval, API approve/verify aliases, browser actions and bulk acceptance/rejection through the same operation. Add rejection and optional reasons, use the selected acting reviewer or explicit CLI/API identity, and submit the candidate the caller actually reviewed. Bulk requests contain per-Goal identities and return individual completed, pending, stale and failed results. Preserve idempotency across browser reloads and transport retries; do not infer the reviewer from the Goal reporter or assignee."
        },
        {
          "id": "P8",
          "description": "Capture settlements at authoritative cancellation, process-stop failure, workflow-attempt failure, exhausted recovery and successful completion boundaries, preserving existing cancellation and stale-worker fences. Record Skill findings and execution errors using invocation/binding identities, candidate, timestamps and structured categories; retain compact durable evidence independent of process logs. Automatic retries and failed Skill attempts alone do not settle the Goal as Failed. Integration and no-required-Skills results remain check/integration facts. An existing configured automatic accept action must use shared proof validation and record its actual invocation, action and pinned configuration authority; otherwise no automatic resolution is classified."
        },
        {
          "id": "P9",
          "description": "Record immutable reopening/supersession events for undo, retry and new Rounds without modifying prior settlements. Count distinct Rounds; count recovery Rounds only from explicit successor lineage, excluding same-Round execution/output retries. Record required operator intervention separately from ordinary acceptance and automatic retry. First-Round success means successful resolution in Round 1 without earlier failed/rejected settlement, a recovery Round or required intervention. Preserve unknown historical lineage or intervention values rather than defaulting them to false."
        },
        {
          "id": "P10",
          "description": "Preserve original audit timestamps and attribution through metadata edits, transfer, synchronization and cache rebuilding. Keep current byte-preserving sync behavior and the existing top-level updated merge rule. Make unchanged bulk/status/metadata requests true no-ops; advance updated and revision for actual semantic changes, including Event receipts. Avoid Round 1's recursive removal of every field named updated when comparing records."
        },
        {
          "id": "P11",
          "description": "Extend application/persistence_sync validation across structural merge, fast-forward/hydration, agent resolution and live/remote recovery. Union independent immutable events by identity; reject same-ID payload changes, missing causal references and incompatible current settlements. Existing authority selection may settle current lifecycle through explicit reconciliation evidence but must retain both original histories. Validate archive coverage before publishing or applying deletion. Preserve ownership rules, retained refs and compare-and-swap publication."
        },
        {
          "id": "P12",
          "description": "Archive a Goal's audit and legacy coverage metadata in synchronized, inspectable durable state before supported Goal, bulk or Feature deletion. Make archive-before-delete restartable and idempotent; failed archival leaves the Goal present. Apply archives before dependent deletions during hydration. Keep decisions, outcomes, recovery lineage and required Skill summaries outside runtime retention. Deduplicate archive/live copies by event identity and preserve history across repeated archival, synchronization and reopening."
        },
        {
          "id": "P13",
          "description": "Extend existing project projections and Event indexes with compact decision, settlement, supersession and coverage entries, date/group lookups and bounded aggregate caches. Update incrementally after local mutations, Skill settlement, synchronization and archival. Use recoverable index-update markers/generations so a crash after a durable record write cannot silently serve stale totals. Rebuild missing/corrupt projections from durable records only as a recovery path; routine queries must not traverse Goal Rounds or invocation histories. Keep schema/derivation in Model, query policy in Application and storage mechanisms in Infrastructure."
        },
        {
          "id": "P14",
          "description": "Expose one shared query through refine metrics and GET /work/metrics using existing HTTP normalization. Support inclusive-start/exclusive-end UTC ranges, day/Monday-week/month buckets and node, Goal-reporter or Feature grouping. Default outcome counts use each Goal's unsuperseded settlement as of the exclusive end, included by completed_at; reopened unresolved Goals have no current settlement. Also return a clearly separate settlement-event series retaining earlier failures/rejections and recovery counts. Human decisions are independently deduplicated and dated by decided_at. Historical grouping uses captured attribution."
        },
        {
          "id": "P15",
          "description": "Define human accept rate as accepted decisions/(accepted+rejected decisions). Define automatic-resolution and terminal-failure rates over classified current terminal Goals in the selected window. Define first-Round success over that population with a known success flag, and average Rounds over records with known total_rounds. Return each numerator, denominator and excluded count; use null for empty denominators. Expose unknown classification, missing dates/attribution, incomplete recovery data and unresolved conflicts. Undated legacy records belong to explicitly unwindowed coverage, never invented time buckets; surviving integration evidence alone cannot establish human acceptance."
        },
        {
          "id": "P16",
          "description": "Add focused behavioral verification for immediate/deferred acceptance and rejection, exact-candidate proof, duplicate and contradictory retries, concurrent stale submissions, pending-gate cancellation, automatic authority, zero required Skills, Skill finding/error followed by recovery, terminal failure, cancellation, same/new-Round reopen, Feature ordering, sync conflicts and archive retention. Inject persistence/index/archive failures and restart between durable-write stages. Verify legacy readability, immutable timestamps/attribution, and browser/CLI/API/bulk parity. Place tests beside their cohesive responsibility rather than expanding existing large service files."
        },
        {
          "id": "P17",
          "description": "Verify known metrics with six classified final Goals: three human accepted, one authorized automatic, one failed and one cancelled; include an earlier rejection followed by acceptance and a Skill-failure recovery without terminal failure. Expect accepted/rejected decision counts 3/1, accept rate 3/4, automatic and failure rates 1/6, first-Round success 2/6 and average Rounds 8/6; the separate settlement history retains the earlier rejection. Add unknown legacy and duplicate archived copies without changing those denominators. Test boundary instants, offsets, leap/month/week boundaries, grouped totals and empty populations. Benchmark cold rebuild separately from warm and incrementally refreshed queries on at least 10,000 multi-Round Goals; instrument zero history-file reads on routine queries and measure against a 50 ms local-query target."
        },
        {
          "id": "P18",
          "description": "Update only affected intent pages for Goal history, Skills transitions, review/done/failed/cancelled/rejected behavior, persistence retention, CLI/API and Goal/Feature surfaces, including the metrics definitions. Verify from the pinned worktree with cargo check --all-targets --locked; cargo test --lib application::work_items -- --test-threads=1; equivalent separate filters for application::events, application::workflow, application::persistence_sync, application::projects::projection, model::workflow, model::feature and surfaces::web_server; cargo test --test sync_regressions --test sync_simulation -- --test-threads=1; and existing xtask test-cli/test-browser/check-static-assets commands. Finish with changed-file formatting checks and git diff --check. Report actual selected test counts, failures, skips, candidate identity and benchmark results; do not claim the proposed checks have already passed."
        }
      ],
      "criticism_resolutions": [
        {
          "criticism_id": "C1",
          "resolution": "The retained attempt predates Skills and cannot be replayed wholesale. P1 and P4 explicitly replace its transition integration while preserving useful source and all Round 1 evidence."
        },
        {
          "criticism_id": "C2",
          "resolution": "Inferring automatic completion from verified integration would manufacture authority. P8 requires the actual configured action and invocation, and excludes passing or absent checks from acceptance."
        },
        {
          "criticism_id": "C3",
          "resolution": "A generic persistence hook can misdate deferred completion or apply stale approval proof. P3-P5 distinguish pending request receipt from atomic decision settlement and revalidate at the deferred boundary."
        },
        {
          "criticism_id": "C4",
          "resolution": "Using only latest Goal outcomes hides recovered failures; counting all settlements as distinct Goals inflates final-resolution rates. P14-P15 expose separately named final-Goal and settlement-event populations with explicit denominators."
        },
        {
          "criticism_id": "C5",
          "resolution": "Round 1's full audit-map aggregation and timestamp-based cache identity do not establish routine query performance or crash consistency. P13 and P17 require indexed selection, recoverable invalidation and measured cold/warm behavior."
        },
        {
          "criticism_id": "C6",
          "resolution": "Blind whole-record authority selection or deletion can discard immutable history. P11-P12 validate retention on every publication/hydration route and make archival a prerequisite for deletion."
        },
        {
          "criticism_id": "C7",
          "resolution": "A log-derived report or separate authoritative database would undermine retention and architectural contracts. The plan keeps audit state with durable work items and synchronized archives, with disposable indexes owned by existing capabilities."
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  "binding_id": "default-plan",
  "evidence": [
    "Observed Round 2 branch refine/DRCBAA3A2FC4ABDDCEC2B87473/round-2 at f880b7767149e4de43d5bc4d4786247d1e536a8c, matching the pinned base and inspected main. Final status showed zero tracked changes and zero untracked files; git diff --check returned exit 0.",
    "Observed retained Round 1 at 8f6de519c62a8a373b19482d5c7842068acfb35d with 38 modified tracked files and 12 untracked files at both inspection points. Read its decision, outcome, archive, merge, metrics, index and test implementations without editing them.",
    "docs/intent/03-application/01-agents/02-skills.md defines current Skill contracts, optional Quality/Governance checks and independent planning. src/application/workflow/phases/quality/service/skill_checks.rs explicitly returns a passing check with no agent checks when no required Skills apply.",
    "src/application/workflow/governance/integration/mod.rs:481 validates exact integration, target ancestry and publication before approval, then calls verify_goal_summary. The latter currently writes Done without a human audit event.",
    "src/application/events/transitions.rs:50 and work_items/service/workflow.rs:7 implement deferred transitions. record_persistence.rs calls prepare_write before durable replacement. Event success actions already carry invocation receipts in events/dispatch.rs.",
    "src/application/work_items/service/workflow_attempts.rs:153 fences authoritative terminal failure by originating Round and attempt. Event invocation storage already maintains history, per-Goal indexes and recoverable index-update markers.",
    "src/application/persistence_sync/state/state_codec.rs:253 copies source bytes without replacing JSON timestamps. Current structural merging treats Rounds as atomic arrays. delete_goal_record currently removes goal.json without outcome archival.",
    "Inspected current workflow, Feature ordering, active-Goal indexes, projection caches, runtime retention, CLI/API/browser adapters and test harnesses. Used intent and authority-boundary analysis, retained-work comparison and self-critique. No implementation tests or benchmarks were run during this observational planning invocation; listed commands are proposed verification."
  ],
  "invocation_id": "e38cfe41790835a44c853b6f8f34a5ddeff70b11cb4edf9274188a3a182ab68b",
